            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0846" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg724"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-10-12"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 12, 1889</date>.
                        (Received November 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 33.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your consideration a copy (in
                    translation) of a note-verbale received in February last from the Sublime Porte,
                    regarding the military service of cavasses and dragomans employed by foreign
                    consulates. (See Legislation Ottomane, Vol. IV, page 16.)</p>
                <p>No reply was made to the Sublime Porte, as this matter was to be considered in
                    union with the other legations and embassies. The matter has received attention,
                    and it has been admitted that the cavasses and dragomans are liable to this
                    service; but there is ambiguity in the text of the regulation, and in my reply I
                    have thought it well to make the reservation seen in the parenthesis.</p>
                <p>I inclose a copy of my proposed reply, which, if it meet your approval, I will
                    send to the Porte.</p>
                <p>I have based it on the note verbale sent by the British embassy, but made it
                    shorter and simpler without omitting (I think) any essential point.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pendleton King.</hi></signed></closer>




